 "text": "Hi there, how can I help you? No problem. How can I help you today? I' sorry to hear that. Dementia can be challenging for both the person with the disease and their family. Can you tell me more about your father's symptoms? That's common in early stage dementia. He may struggle with finding words, losing track of time, or feeling agitated. It' a good idea to prepare for his visit by creating a schedule and making sure you have his favorite foods, medications, and any other essentials. Yes? It's natural to feel that way. But remember, you're taking care of your father, not just a guest. Be kind to yourself and take breaks when you need them. It' okay to admit when you're overwhelmed.",
